From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bringup <bringup@t1100.local>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:00:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/mediatek: dsi: take the per-lane rate limit from the
 driver data

mtk_dsi_bridge_mode_valid() rejected every mode whose per-lane bit rate
exceeds 1.5 Gbps, hard-coded for all SoCs. The T1100 panel is
1600x2176@60 RGB888 on 4 lanes:

  (1600+109+34+10) * (2176+220+28+8) * 60 = 255797 kHz pixel clock
  255797 kHz * 24 bpp / 4 lanes           = 1534788 kbps per lane

so the only mode the panel reports would be dropped and every atomic
commit would fail with MODE_CLOCK_HIGH, even though the MT8183/MT6771
MIPI TX PLL runs undivided (txdiv = 1) for data rates at or above
2 Gbps, see mtk_mipi_tx_pll_enable() in
drivers/phy/mediatek/phy-mtk-mipi-dsi-mt8183.c.

Add a per-SoC max_lane_rate to mtk_dsi_driver_data, keep the previous
1.5 Gbps where it is not set (mt8173, mt2701) and give the mt8183 data
(which is also what MT6771 binds through) 2 Gbps.

The MT6771 MIPI TX block is the same as MT8183's (stock T1100 DT:
mipi_tx0@11e50000, same registers; the port uses mt8183.dtsi), so the
MT8183 number applies. To be verified on hardware: if the PLL fails to
lock at 1.535 Gbps the DSI output stays dark and the fix is to lower
the mode clock, not to raise this limit.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c | 21 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
index 796113933..f8da5999a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
@@ -194,6 +194,8 @@ struct mtk_dsi_driver_data {
 	bool has_size_ctl;
 	bool cmdq_long_packet_ctl;
 	bool support_per_frame_lp;
+	/* Maximum per-lane bit rate in kbps, 0 means the historical 1.5 Gbps. */
+	u32 max_lane_rate;
 };
 
 struct mtk_dsi {
@@ -875,13 +877,24 @@ mtk_dsi_bridge_mode_valid(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 			  const struct drm_display_mode *mode)
 {
 	struct mtk_dsi *dsi = bridge_to_dsi(bridge);
+	u32 max_rate;
 	int bpp;
 
 	bpp = mipi_dsi_pixel_format_to_bpp(dsi->format);
 	if (bpp < 0)
 		return MODE_ERROR;
 
-	if (mode->clock * bpp / dsi->lanes > 1500000)
+	/*
+	 * mode->clock is the pixel clock in kHz, so this is the per-lane bit
+	 * rate in kbps. The MT8183/MT6771 MIPI TX PLL runs with txdiv = 1
+	 * (see mtk_mipi_tx_pll_enable() in
+	 * drivers/phy/mediatek/phy-mtk-mipi-dsi-mt8183.c) for anything at or
+	 * above 2 Gbps, so the old hard-coded 1.5 Gbps per lane rejected the
+	 * 1600x2176@60 RGB888 4-lane mode of the T1100 panel, which needs
+	 * 1600+109+34+10 x 2176+220+28+8 x 60 x 24 / 4 = 1534788 kbps.
+	 */
+	max_rate = dsi->driver_data->max_lane_rate ?: 1500000;
+	if (mode->clock * bpp / dsi->lanes > max_rate)
 		return MODE_CLOCK_HIGH;
 
 	return MODE_OK;
@@ -1290,6 +1303,12 @@ static const struct mtk_dsi_driver_data mt8183_dsi_driver_data = {
 	.reg_shadow_dbg_off = 0x190,
 	.has_shadow_ctl = true,
 	.has_size_ctl = true,
+	/*
+	 * The MT8183/MT6771 MIPI TX PLL handles up to 2 Gbps per lane without
+	 * a post divider; keep some headroom above that for the 1600x2176
+	 * panel (1.535 Gbps) while staying inside the documented PLL range.
+	 */
+	.max_lane_rate = 2000000,
 };
 
 static const struct mtk_dsi_driver_data mt8186_dsi_driver_data = {
